  "worked_solution": "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=-1.5$ and $x=0.5.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2$ between the lower limit $x=-1.5$ and the upper limit $x=0.5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-1.5}^{0.5}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
